Me:
what is openrouter.ai and how is it different from using ollama locally

AI: 
OpenRouter is a cloud service that gives you access to many AI models through a single API — including GPT-3.5, GPT-4, Claude, and others. You send requests to https://openrouter.ai/api and it routes them to whichever model you specify.
Ollama runs AI models locally on a machine. The university had an Ollama server at ollama.serveur.au that hosted llama3.2. When that server is unreachable you cannot use it.
OpenRouter is more reliable for a student project because it is a commercial service with uptime guarantees. You pay per API call but the costs are very low for a project of this size. The hands-on-ai package supports both — you just change the HANDS_ON_AI_SERVER and HANDS_ON_AI_MODEL environment variables.

