Me:
what is the hands-on-ai python package and what can it do

AI:
hands-on-ai is a Python teaching package that wraps LLM API calls into simple functions designed for students learning AI-powered programming. It provides three main capabilities for your project. The chat module gives you get_response() which sends a message to the language model and returns the reply. The RAG module gives you get_answer() which retrieves an answer from a document you provide. The agent module lets you register Python functions as tools the LLM can call. All three connect to the Ollama server at ollama.serveur.au using your API key, so you do not need to manage API connections yourself.

Me:
explain RAG to me like i have never heard of it before, use my finance project as the example

AI:
RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation. You give the AI a specific document to read and tell it to only answer from what is written in that document.

Without RAG: the user asks "how do I spend less on tea?" and the AI answers from general knowledge with vague tips.

With RAG: the user asks "how do I spend less on tea?" and the AI reads your FINANCIAL_TIPS document first, finds the section about Tea and Café, and answers with the specific advice from that section — for example "Brew tea at home more often" and "Limit daily café visits.

The key benefit is that the answers are grounded in your specific document, not in whatever the model was trained on.

