in my notebook the rag_lookup function does not use hands_on_ai.rag, it just passes the document in the system prompt and calls get_response, is that still RAG

AI:
Yes, what your notebook does is a simplified form of RAG called prompt-based retrieval. Instead of a vector database that searches for relevant chunks, you include the entire FINANCIAL_TIPS document directly in the system prompt and instruct the model to only answer from it. For a small document like yours this works perfectly well. The instruction "Answer ONLY using the document below" combined with "If the answer is not found in the document, say so" ensures the model stays grounded in your content. It is simpler to implement and just as effective for a knowledge base of this size.
